{
  "_comment": "The controlled vocabulary api/tags.py reads the ERP's itineraryTags with. Each attribute is a list of rules in priority order: a tag matches a rule when it holds one of the rule's substrings, and the first rule a tag matches is the one it counts for. A tag holding one of the attribute's negative substrings counts for nothing there. destination and departure_city keep every value they match, in the order the tags carry them; the others keep one value, the earliest rule any tag matched. A place name that sits inside another place's name is claimed by whichever rule is listed first, so the destinations run from the specific to the general: 罗马尼亚 and 布加勒斯特 stand above 罗马 and 加勒, 都柏林 above 柏林, 菲斯特 above 菲斯, 马拉喀什 above 喀什. A tag that names a dish or a square rather than a place is a negative: 土耳其烤肉卷 is a meal on a European line and 西班牙广场 is in Rome. Product staff extend this file; no code changes with it. The region attribute (线路系) is read off the 线路 name first and its tags only when the name says nothing, so a 德法意瑞 line whose tags list 意大利 is not 意大利一地; its rules go from the more specific walk to the less (西欧多国 before 德法意瑞 before 法意瑞).",
